{
  "question": "Why does pendulum_lab exhibit a strong 3-day-lagged correlation (r = 0.820) with resonator_obs—two physically distinct instruments measuring different phenomena in the same lab—while pendulum_obs, which should measure the same pendulum physics as pendulum_lab, shows almost zero correlation with either lab stream and instead displays persistent unidirectional drift? What is the source of the synchronized oscillation in pendulum_lab and resonator_obs, and why does pendulum_obs decouple from it?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "Pendulum_obs exhibits independent systematic error (calibration drift, optical aberration, mechanical creep, or post-day-10 protocol shift) separate from true pendulum physics; pendulum_lab and resonator_obs respond to environmental forcing at 3–7 day quasi-period",
