      "rationale": "Pendulum_obs alone shows statistically significant unidirectional drift (z = −2.21 post-baseline; z = −2.01 over 28 days; today's 16 trials mean 2.5011, consonant with established trend events 26165, 257072, 750266, 957527, 185255, 220892, 768077, 824656, 584770, 82176, 322608, 888393, 26182, 290935, 372069, 111027). Critically, pendulum_lab—measuring the identical physical system via different observational protocol—remains stable (z = −1.04, non-significant). This dissociation isolates error to pendulum_obs measurement chain rather than pendulum physics. Resonator_obs shows only marginal drift (z = −1.58), nearly identical to pendulum_lab's drift magnitude, suggesting both lab instruments participate in the same environmental response rather than independent instrumental error. The three-day-lagged sync between pendulum_lab (z = −1.04 drift, decoupled from pendulum_obs) and resonator_obs (r = 0.820 at 3-day lag, n=102, well above chance 0.287, events 145026, 188796, 750266, 906693, 171740, 104305, 948796, 630572, 918846) indicates organized forcing affecting both lab instruments via shared environmental pathway (temperature, pressure, optical coupling). Pendulum_obs contamination by independent error would mask its participation in this cycle, explaining why it shows pure drift uncorrelated with either lab stream (pendulum_lab ↔ pendulum_obs r = 0.151 at 6-day offset, events 26165, 257072, 750266, 957527, 185255, 220892; pendulum_obs ↔ resonator_obs r = 0.172 at 0-day offset, both within chance). Autocorrelations in pendulum_lab (lag-6, r = 0.305) and resonator_obs (lag-13, r = 0.261) suggest quasi-periodic environmental forcing independent of instrumental drift. Two-process model: (1) environment drives 3–7 day cycle in lab instruments; (2) pendulum_obs-specific systematic error accumulates continuously, suppressing oscillatory signal. Today's data raise probability from 0.51 to 0.58 because the consistency of pendulum_obs drift over 40 days without any hint of phase-locked oscillation—despite 25 new independent trials—strengthens the case that pendulum_obs and lab streams operate under fundamentally different regimes. No new environmental anomalies detected in today's resonator_obs readings (events 906693, 171740, 104305, 948796, 630572, 918846) that would suggest decay or shift in forcing.",
