      "rationale": "The pendulum_lab ↔ resonator_obs correlation emerges from a search over ~24 comparisons (6 instrument pairs, multiple lags). With such a large lag-search space, a false-positive correlation r = 0.820 at one lag is plausible under the null hypothesis of independent noise. All other cross-instrument correlations cluster near chance (range −0.167 to 0.202, chance thresholds ±0.265–0.316), suggesting the high pendulum_lab ↔ resonator_obs value is an outlier. Autocorrelations (range −0.262 to 0.305) are mostly weak, inconsistent with strong periodic forcing. Pendulum_obs drift (z = −2.01) could reflect small-sample regression or transient excursion. Today's 25 additional readings do not provide new lag-structure data to test the oscillation hypothesis independently; they merely reinforce the existing downward drift in pendulum_obs, which is compatible with noise. However, probability is lowered from 0.08 to 0.07 because: (i) the dataset now spans 40 days with ~968 trial-days across four streams, reducing small-sample noise concern; (ii) lag-6 and lag-13 echoes appear consistently within individual streams (pendulum_lab lag-6 r = 0.305, pendulum_obs lag-13 r = 0.275, resonator_lab lag-14 r = 0.350, resonator_obs lag-13 r = 0.218), suggesting real autocorrelation structure rather than one-off alignment; (iii) the fact that three independent streams (pendulum_lab, resonator_lab, resonator_obs) all show marginal drifts (z = −0.84 to −1.59) while one stream alone (pendulum_obs) shows significant drift argues against global noise or artifact. Probability remains non-negligible (0.07) because independent replication in a separate dataset is essential before claiming detection of the 3-day cycle.",
